"]}, "overview": "Tennessee remains one of the most Republican states in presidential voting, and the 2028 race features no incumbent after the term-limited president leaves office. Recent cycles have produced double-digit Republican wins, and the state's partisan lean points to a margin of roughly fourteen points for the Republican nominee. No public general-election polls or expert ratings are available, so the forecast rests on fundamentals alone.\n\nHeadlines offer mixed signals. The president's approval has slipped below fifty percent even in Tennessee, a mild drag on his party, while Republican redistricting that eliminated the state's last Democratic-leaning congressional district underscores the party's structural strength. With no polling to refine the picture, uncertainty stays wide, but the fundamentals make a Democratic upset a long shot.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0603, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1012, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.11, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1055, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0961, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1038, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0969, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1086, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.082, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0965, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1008, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0993, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0988, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1057, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0921, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0979, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.104, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0893, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.08, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_d